  "about": "PrivatePaste E2E cross-client test vectors (protocol 2), generated by tests/PrivatePaste.Tests/Protocol/VaultCryptoTests.cs with PP_WRITE_VECTORS=1. All byte values are lowercase hex unless the field name says otherwise. vaultKey: vk (32-byte vault key) -> encKey, hashKey (HKDF-SHA256, no salt, info 'privatepaste v1 enc' / 'privatepaste v1 hash') and keyId (first 8 bytes of HKDF info 'privatepaste v1 key id'). payload: small item 0x01 || nonce || ciphertext || tag under encKey with AAD 'privatepaste v1 ' + purpose; json is the UTF-8 plaintext, sealed the full output. blob: chunked format 0x02 || noncePrefix, then 1 MiB chunks; plaintext byte i = i % 251 for plaintextLength bytes; only SHA-256 digests and the length of the output are stored. emptyBlob: the full output for an empty plaintext (one final chunk). keyedHash: text -> contentHash (ContentHash.ForText) -> keyedHash = HMAC-SHA256(hashKey, UTF-8 of contentHash). fileHash: ContentHash.ForFiles: SHA-256 over UTF-8 'f:' then per file name + NUL + decimal size + NUL + sha256Hex(content) + LF; expected is lowercase hex. safeFileName: FileNames.Safe(in) = out (untrusted payload name -> safe leaf name). fileSize: FileNames.FormatSize(bytes) = text (integer half-up rounding: tenths = (bytes*10 + unit/2) / unit; one decimal only below 10 and not .0; a KB value rounding to 1024 is shown as MB). fileRowText: FileNames.RowText(files) = text (the first name is shown as its safeFileName). Safe: the 200-unit cut steps back one unit rather than split a surrogate pair, then trims trailing dots and spaces from the stem (empty stem -> file). Then, if the UTF-8 length is over 200 bytes, the stem is cut to fit 200 bytes with the extension by whole code points (a surrogate pair counts 4 bytes, a lone surrogate 3); an extension over 32 bytes is cut with the stem as one; trailing dots and spaces are trimmed again (empty stem -> file). handover: blob is otk-sealed small item with AAD 'privatepaste v1 handover' and plaintext vk; qrText uses id, base64url otk without padding, and keyId. handoverUrlSafe: a second handover whose otk text contains - and _. thumb: a small item with purpose thumb; plaintext is hex. argon2: passphrase (NFC-normalised, UTF-8) -> 32-byte key with the given salt and cost; the NFC and NFD spellings of the same text give the same key. passphraseWrap: the VK wrapped under a passphrase: AES-256-GCM with AAD 'privatepaste v1 vault ' + keyId under the argon2 key (salt 0..15, 64 MiB, 3, 1); wrap is the VaultWrap DTO as sent on the wire (base64).",
